# Keep Vercel on the classic static + /api serverless-functions model.
#
# Vercel CLI 59+ treats a root pyproject.toml as a single-entrypoint Python
# "backend framework", which conflicts with our two independent /api functions.
# Hiding the Python packaging files from the Vercel build (they are only needed
# for local install / CI) restores classic detection: public/ is served
# statically and each api/*.py is its own serverless function. The functions
# install their deps from api/requirements.txt and bundle the stock_comber
# source via the includeFiles glob in vercel.json.
pyproject.toml
requirements.txt

# Nothing below is needed at the edge.
tests/
docs/
config/
stock_comber.egg-info/
reports/screen-*
.github/
